                      "text": "I'll bind the generative model to its inference serving contract by recording the model identifier and endpoint, with some light validation of the contract fields.\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom urllib.parse import urlparse\n\n# --- Declared serving contract inputs ---\nmodel_identifier = \"synthetic-review-summarizer-v1\"\nserving_endpoint = \"https://inference.example.com/v1/chat/completions\"\n\n# --- Validate / normalize the endpoint ---\nparsed = urlparse(serving_endpoint)\nendpoint_valid = all([parsed.scheme == \"https\", bool(parsed.netloc), parsed.path.endswith(\"/v1/chat/completions\")])\n\n# --- Bind model -> serving contract ---\nbinding = {\n    \"effective_model_name\": model_identifier,\n    \"endpoint\": serving_endpoint,\n    \"endpoint_host\": parsed.netloc,\n    \"endpoint_path\": parsed.path,\n    \"transport\": parsed.scheme,\n    \"api_style\": \"openai-compatible chat completions\",\n    \"endpoint_valid\": endpoint_valid,\n    \"contract_status\": \"bound\" if endpoint_valid else \"invalid_endpoint\",\n}\n\ncontract_df = pd.DataFrame([binding]).set_index(\"effective_model_name\")\nprint(contract_df.T)\n```\n\nThis produces the bound contract below.\n\nLet me run it to confirm the output.",
